//? Title: Soft actor-critic on articulated vsim tasks
//? Lang: en

> Soft actor-critic on articulated vsim tasks

Soft actor-critic fits a stochastic actor, two value critics, and an
entropy temperature from a replay buffer. The target uses the lower
of the two target critics and includes the next action’s entropy
bonus. Only physical termination masks the bootstrap. The target
critics follow exponential moving averages of the fitted critics.

The actor samples Gaussian actions and applies tanh to keep them in
the unit box. The simulator receives actions scaled to its actuator
limits. Evaluation uses the deterministic tanh of the Gaussian mean.
The rollout footage uses this mean policy, filmed on the highest-return
of three seeded trials.

The pendulum protocol uses 30,000 transitions. The longer Hopper
protocol uses 300,000. Both use 256-unit layers, 256-sample replay
batches, and 1,000 warmup actions. The C++ code accepts `DM_SAC_TASK`
to select one task and `DM_SAC_STEPS` to set a smaller experimental
budget. Datamunge initializes its own model parameters.

> Run with the vsim SDK

Use the [vsim SDK and original scenes|../6.1_environments/vsim_articulated_tasks.mepml]
setup. The same compiler flags enable the task adapter and link the
offscreen renderer. The run publishes one chart and one video per task.

```{cpp, results="output", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) $(echo ${DM_VSIM_TASK_FLAGS:-}) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#if defined(DATAMUNGE_ENABLE_VSIM_TASKS)
#include <vsim/renderer.hpp>

namespace n=dm::nn;
namespace e=dm::rl::environments;
namespace m=n::models;

void train_sac(vsim::Renderer& renderer,const std::filesystem::path& scenes,e::VsimTask task,int steps) {
  const bool pendulum=task==e::VsimTask::InvertedPendulum;
  const std::string name=pendulum?"inverted_pendulum":"hopper";
  e::VsimTaskEnv env(task,scenes/(name+".json")), test(task,scenes/(name+".json"));
  const auto space=env.action_space();
  const int dimension=space.dim, features=env.obs_size();
  constexpr int batch=256, width=256, warmup=1000;
  n::ParameterStore actor(0), critic(1), target(2), temperature(3);
  const auto log_alpha=temperature.get("log_alpha",{},n::init::zeros());
  const auto policy=[&](const n::Tensor& state) { return m::GaussianActor(actor,"pi",state,dimension,width); };
  const auto q=[](n::ParameterStore& store,const char* key,const n::Tensor& state,const n::Tensor& action) {
    return m::QNetwork(store,key,state,action,width);
  };
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    const auto state=n::zeros({1,features}), action=n::zeros({1,dimension});
    policy(state);
    for(auto* store:{&critic,&target})
      for(const char* key:{"q1","q2"}) q(*store,key,state,action);
    target.copy_from(critic,1.);
  }
  n::Optimizer actor_opt(actor,.0003,{.kind=n::OptimizerKind::Adam});
  n::Optimizer critic_opt(critic,.0003,{.kind=n::OptimizerKind::Adam});
  n::Optimizer alpha_opt(temperature,.0003,{.kind=n::OptimizerKind::Adam});
  dm::rl::replay::ReplayBuffer replay(100000,features);
  std::mt19937_64 rng(0);
  const auto noise=[&](int rows) {
    std::normal_distribution<float> normal;
    std::vector<float> values(rows*dimension);
    for(auto& value:values) value=normal(rng);
    return n::from_vector(values,{rows,dimension});
  };
  const auto act=[&](const e::Obs& observed,bool random) {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    const auto distribution=policy(n::from_vector(observed,{1,features}));
    return (random?m::SquashedSample(distribution,noise(1)).action:n::tanh(distribution.mean))
        .to_vector<float>();
  };
  const auto scale=[&](std::vector<float> unit) {
    for (int j=0;j<dimension;++j)
      unit[j]=space.low[j]+(unit[j]+1.f)*.5f*(space.high[j]-space.low[j]);
    return e::Action(std::move(unit));
  };
  const auto evaluate=[&](int seed) {
    auto observed=test.reset(seed);
    float reward=0;
    while(true) {
      auto result=test.step(scale(act(observed,false)));
      reward+=result.reward;
      if(result.done()) return reward;
      observed=std::move(result.obs);
    }
  };
  const auto mean_return=[&](int first,int count) {
    double total=0;
    for(int i=0;i<count;++i) total+=evaluate(first+i);
    return total/count;
  };
  const double initial=mean_return(777,10);
  std::vector<double> eval_steps{0}, evaluations{initial}, log_steps, losses, temperatures;
  double interval_loss=0;
  int interval_updates=0;
  auto observed=env.reset(0);
  int updates=0, episodes=0;
  for (int step=1;step<=steps;++step) {
    std::vector<float> unit;
    if (step<=warmup) {
      unit.resize(dimension);
      for (auto& u:unit) u=std::uniform_real_distribution<float>(-1,1)(rng);
    } else {
      unit=act(observed,true);
    }
    auto result=env.step(scale(unit));
    replay.Add({observed,0,result.reward,result.obs,result.terminated?1.f:0.f,unit});
    observed=result.done()?env.reset():std::move(result.obs);
    episodes+=result.done();
    if (step>warmup) {
      const auto samples=replay.Sample(batch,rng);
      const auto eps=noise(batch), eps_next=noise(batch);
      const auto alpha=n::exp(log_alpha).detach();
      n::Tensor y;
      {
        n::NoGradGuard guard;
        const auto next=m::SquashedSample(policy(samples.s2),eps_next);
        const auto soft_q=n::minimum(q(target,"q1",samples.s2,next.action),
                                    q(target,"q2",samples.s2,next.action))-alpha*next.logp;
        y=samples.r+(.99f*(1.f-samples.done))*soft_q;
      }
      const auto loss=n::mean(n::square(y-q(critic,"q1",samples.s,samples.act_c)))+
                      n::mean(n::square(y-q(critic,"q2",samples.s,samples.act_c)));
      critic_opt.minimize(loss);
      const auto sample=m::SquashedSample(policy(samples.s),eps);
      const auto soft_min=n::minimum(q(critic,"q1",samples.s,sample.action),q(critic,"q2",samples.s,sample.action));
      actor_opt.minimize(n::mean(alpha*sample.logp-soft_min));
      alpha_opt.minimize(-n::mean(log_alpha*(sample.logp.detach()-dimension)));
      target.copy_from(critic,.005f);
      interval_loss+=loss.item();
      ++interval_updates;
      ++updates;
    }
    if (step%4000==0) {
      evaluations.push_back(mean_return(1000+step,5));
      eval_steps.push_back(step);
    }
    if ((step%2000==0 || step==steps) && interval_updates) {
      log_steps.push_back(step);
      losses.push_back(interval_loss/interval_updates);
      temperatures.push_back(n::exp(log_alpha).item());
      if (!std::isfinite(losses.back()) || !std::isfinite(temperatures.back()))
        throw std::runtime_error("nonfinite SAC update");
      interval_loss=0;
      interval_updates=0;
      std::println("{} step {} critic loss {:.5f} alpha {:.5f}",name,step,losses.back(),temperatures.back());
      std::cout.flush();
    }
  }
  if (updates!=steps-warmup) throw std::runtime_error("unexpected SAC update count");
  const double final=mean_return(777,10);
  if (eval_steps.back()==steps) evaluations.back()=final;
  else { eval_steps.push_back(steps); evaluations.push_back(final); }
  std::println("{}: {} transitions, {} updates, {} episodes, return {:.2f} -> {:.2f}",
               name,steps,updates,episodes,initial,final);
  auto eval_plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  eval_plot.lines(eval_steps,evaluations,"Mean policy",{37,99,235})
      .title("Deterministic evaluation").x_label("Transitions").y_label("Mean return");
  auto critic_plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  critic_plot.lines(log_steps,losses,"Twin critic",{204,99,42})
      .title("Soft Bellman loss").x_label("Transitions").y_label("Squared error");
  auto alpha_plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  alpha_plot.lines(log_steps,temperatures,"Temperature",{39,130,92})
      .title("Entropy temperature").x_label("Transitions").y_label("Alpha");
  const auto publish=[](const std::string& file) {
    std::filesystem::copy_file("build/"+file,"figures/"+file,std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  };
  const int full_budget=pendulum?30000:300000;
  const auto stem="sac_vsim_trained_"+name+(steps==full_budget?"":"_"+std::to_string(steps));
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,3).add(eval_plot).add(critic_plot).add(alpha_plot)
      .size(1220,420).fit_panels().save_svg("build/"+stem+".svg");
  publish(stem+".svg");
  actor.save("build/"+stem+"_actor.npz");
  int best_seed=4242;
  float best=-std::numeric_limits<float>::infinity();
  for(int seed=4242;seed<4245;++seed)
    if(const auto reward=evaluate(seed);reward>best) { best=reward; best_seed=seed; }
  constexpr int w=640,h=400;
  dm::cad::VideoWriter video("build/"+stem+".mp4",w,h,pendulum?25:62);
  dm::cad::RenderResult frame;
  frame.width=w;
  frame.height=h;
  vsim::Image image{};
  vsim::RenderView view;
  observed=test.reset(best_seed);
  for(int i=1;i<=(pendulum?750:1000);++i) {
    auto result=test.step(scale(act(observed,false)));
    if(pendulum || i%2==0 || result.done()) {
      const auto x=test.root_position().x;
      const auto offset=pendulum?glm::vec3(0,.55f,3.2f):glm::vec3(.8f,1.3f,4.2f);
      view.transform.position=glm::vec3(x,0,0)+offset;
      const auto look=glm::vec3(x+offset.x,pendulum?.15f:.75f,0);
      view.transform.rotation=glm::quatLookAtRH(glm::normalize(look-view.transform.position),glm::vec3(0,1,0));
      view.camera.vertical_fov=pendulum?40:38;
      if(!renderer.draw(test.scene(),&view)) throw std::runtime_error("vsim draw failed");
      renderer.capture(image);
      frame.rgba.swap(image.rgba);
      video.append(frame);
      frame.rgba.swap(image.rgba);
    }
    if(result.done()) break;
    observed=std::move(result.obs);
  }
  video.finish();
  publish(stem+".mp4");
  std::println("{}: recorded {} frames, best seed {} full return {:.2f}",name,video.frames_written(),best_seed,best);
}
#endif

int main() {
#if defined(DATAMUNGE_ENABLE_VSIM_TASKS)
  const auto* scenes=std::getenv("DM_VSIM_SCENES");
  if(!scenes || !*scenes) throw std::runtime_error("set DM_VSIM_SCENES to the authored scene directory");
  const auto* task=std::getenv("DM_SAC_TASK");
  const std::string_view selection=task?task:"both";
  if(selection!="both" && selection!="inverted_pendulum" && selection!="hopper")
    throw std::invalid_argument("DM_SAC_TASK must be both, inverted_pendulum, or hopper");
  const auto* override_text=std::getenv("DM_SAC_STEPS");
  const int budget=override_text?std::stoi(override_text):0;
  if(override_text && budget<=1000) throw std::invalid_argument("DM_SAC_STEPS must exceed warmup");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  vsim::Renderer renderer({.width=640,.height=400,.offscreen=true});
  if(selection!="hopper") train_sac(renderer,scenes,e::VsimTask::InvertedPendulum,budget?budget:30000);
  if(selection!="inverted_pendulum") train_sac(renderer,scenes,e::VsimTask::Hopper,budget?budget:300000);
#else
  std::puts("Set DM_VSIM_TASK_FLAGS and DM_VSIM_SCENES for the SDK-backed experiment.");
#endif
}
```
// result_begin:
// inverted_pendulum step 1100 critic loss 1.59372 alpha 0.97054
// inverted_pendulum: 1100 transitions, 100 updates, 111 episodes, return 26.90 -> 16.10
// inverted_pendulum: recorded 22 frames, best seed 4243 full return 22.00
// hopper step 1100 critic loss 3.07169 alpha 0.97024
// hopper: 1100 transitions, 100 updates, 109 episodes, return 11.46 -> 68.44
// hopper: recorded 40 frames, best seed 4244 full return 70.15
// result_end


> Recorded 1,100-transition check

Each run completed 100 optimizer updates after warmup. The mean
return fell from 26.90 to 16.10 for InvertedPendulum and rose from
11.46 to 68.44 for Hopper. This run checks the training, evaluation,
and video paths. At this budget the pendulum still falls quickly.

\image(figures/sac_vsim_trained_inverted_pendulum_1100.svg)
\caption(InvertedPendulum evaluation, critic loss, and temperature after the short run.)

\video(figures/sac_vsim_trained_inverted_pendulum_1100.mp4)
\caption(InvertedPendulum mean policy after 100 updates.)

\image(figures/sac_vsim_trained_hopper_1100.svg)
\caption(Hopper evaluation, critic loss, and temperature after the short run.)

\video(figures/sac_vsim_trained_hopper_1100.mp4)
\caption(Hopper mean policy after 100 updates.)

> Full pendulum schedule

After 30,000 transitions and 29,000 updates, the ten-episode mean
return increased from 26.90 to 1,000. The selected policy video covers
750 steps at 25 fps. The selected seed reaches the full 1,000-step
horizon when evaluated without the recording cap.

\image(figures/sac_vsim_trained_inverted_pendulum.svg)
\caption(Deterministic evaluation, critic loss, and temperature over the full pendulum fit.)

\video(figures/sac_vsim_trained_inverted_pendulum.mp4)
\caption(The trained pendulum policy holds balance throughout the recorded interval.)

> Full Hopper schedule

After 300,000 transitions and 299,000 updates, the ten-episode mean
return increased from 11.46 to 261.81. The best of the three recording
seeds returned 261.47. The clip captures every second simulation step
and the final terminal frame at 62 fps.

\image(figures/sac_vsim_trained_hopper.svg)
\caption(Deterministic evaluation, critic loss, and temperature over the full Hopper fit.)

\video(figures/sac_vsim_trained_hopper.mp4)
\caption(Hopper’s deterministic policy after the full training schedule.)
